source	Thomas Aquinas, Summa Theologica I q.19 a.8 obj. 3, tr. Fathers of the English Dominican Province
text	Project Gutenberg ebook 17611, https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/17611
class	scope
word	necessary
fault	that the conditional "if God wills a thing, it comes to pass" is necessary gives the necessity of the consequence; that what God wills is necessary absolutely needs the necessity of the consequent
reference	Aquinas, ST I q.19 a.8 ad 3 (consequents have necessity according to the mode of their antecedents)
known	canon
